  "label": "User projected onto the cat as a stand-in for a Jew",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the cat, which is visually depicted as a stand-in for a Jew according to the antisemitic stereotype embedded in the meme. The text 'you're a cat, not a jew' directly addresses the viewer, implying that the viewer (user) is being told to recognize the cat as a Jew, thereby projecting the user's identity onto the cat as the target of the antisemitic trope. The user is thus projected onto the visual material (the cat) through the textual material's deictic address.",
